course: dictionary
lesson: 11796
title: Proper nouns: the Bennet family
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bennet is a family name. A name like this starts with a capital letter, because it names one particular family, not any family.
explain: «The Bennet family lived in a house in the country with their five daughters.» Here Bennet is the surname that all the family members share, like Mr Bennet and Mrs Bennet.
explain: «Elizabeth Bennet is the clever, bold heroine of Pride and Prejudice, a famous novel by Jane Austen.» Bennet is a proper noun, so it names one specific family or person. Ask yourself: is this a special name for one thing, or a general word for many things?
explain: Bennet has a second, rare meaning: herb bennet, a wild plant with small yellow flowers, also called wood avens. You will almost never meet it in stories, so check a dictionary if you do.
fact: Bennet is a family name, best known as the Bennet family in Jane Austen's novel «Pride and Prejudice».
fact: «Elizabeth Bennet» is the clever main character of that novel.
fact: Mr and Mrs Bennet have five daughters, so the Bennet sisters are a big family in the story.
fact: Bennet is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Rare: herb bennet is a wild plant with yellow flowers, also called wood avens.
exercise: «The Bennet family lived near a small town.» What kind of word is Bennet here? | A month of the year | A large house | *A family name | A kind of animal
exercise: «Elizabeth Bennet was clever and brave.» Who is Elizabeth Bennet? | A king from long ago | A wild plant with yellow flowers | *A character in Pride and Prejudice | A town in the north
exercise: Why does Bennet start with a capital letter? | It is always written in bold | It means a happy day | It is a colour word | *It is the name of a particular family
test: «The five Bennet daughters went to the ball together.» How many Bennet daughters are there? | *Five | Seven | Six | Three
test: In herb bennet, the rare plant, what colour are the flowers? | Blue | White | *Yellow | Red
exam: «Elizabeth Bennet is the heroine of Pride and Prejudice.» What kind of word is Bennet? | *A proper noun naming a family | A verb meaning to talk | An adjective describing a person | A common noun for a plant
